│ {"study_index": 10, "title": "Review of incidence studies of tardive dyskinesia associated with typical              │
│ antipsychotics", "abstract": "Unless researchers make an organized effort, patients with tardive dyskinesia are      │
│ difficult to study and easily lost to follow up. Because there is no treatment for tardive dyskinesia, investigators │
│ are obliged to study the natural history of the disorder and identify risk and prognostic factors to further         │
│ understand pathophysiologic mechanisms and to guide prevention and treatment efforts. Abundant variability exists    │
│ among incidence studies of tardive dyskinesia, depending to some extent on design issues. In this article, the       │
│ design concepts of incidence and prevalence studies are described, along with results, methodological problems, and  │
